tent" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-20_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-21_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-22_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-23_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="713a47e8-a30f-4093-8b7d-34049d567bee" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> Is the rear camera waterproof?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-25_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-26_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-27_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-eab07d87-c696-405c-ad5a-9c12995ae268"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">No. The rear camera is <strong>not waterproof</strong> and is recommended to be installed <strong>inside the vehicle</strong>.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-30_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-31_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="7f1b7285-1e3f-42be-b712-d6cf1a40f18d" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How long is each recorded video?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-33_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-34_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-35_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-a2a2343f-b20d-41b3-ab08-e53564148bf0"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">The dash cam supports loop recording with selectable clip lengths of <strong>1 minute, 3 minutes, or 5 minutes.</strong></span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-38_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-39_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="d7861052-afb3-45fd-ba3f-603193040c79" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>What temperature does the dash cam support?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-41_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-42_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-43_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-32114be6-ed95-40d1-b606-f7f397bc0eef"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">The working temperature range is <strong>-20°C to 70°C</strong>, suitable for most vehicle environments.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-46_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-47_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="a39abcd9-ad20-4123-a56a-658d64402769" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>What is the parking mode of the dash cam? And how does it work?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-49_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-50_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-51_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-22937a12-22a8-4865-a495-be39414f796d"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Parking Mode requires a<strong> Type-C hardwire kit (not included)</strong>. When enabled, the camera monitors the vehicle while parked and automatically records and locks video if a collision is detected.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-54_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-55_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="ad5d6afa-ef7d-4e19-8b64-3ee5e83693cb" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>What type of fuse does the hardware kit have?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-57_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-58_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-59_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-ef7d9e19-cb64-4ee5-a836-93cb5577069a"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">The hardwire kit supports common vehicle fuse types. Compatibility depends on the vehicle model. We recommend our brand's hardwiring kits.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-62_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-63_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="c3175285-1a91-4330-96f7-ab78f704b3e8" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>What is loop-recording? And how does it work?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-65_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-66_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-67_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-1a912330-96f7-4b78-b704-b3e8e2ab1ca4"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> Loop recording automatically overwrites the oldest normal video files when the memory card is full. Locked emergency videos will not be overwritten.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-70_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-71_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="7b8bdafc-f92d-4a9c-9266-4622a8eee7f6" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why only 1/3/5 minutes can be selected on the dash cam? Can’t record for a long time?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-73_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-74_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-75_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-f92d9a9c-d266-4622-a8ee-e7f6c7aa61e3"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Short video segments help ensure file integrity and stable playback. Continuous single-file recording is not supported by design.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-78_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-79_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="362453af-c0be-46c0-b542-56f833dd6ec6" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> Does the recorded video have sound?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-81_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-82_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-83_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-c0be86c0-f542-46f8-b3dd-6ec67c21eb31"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Yes. Audio recording is enabled by default and can be turned off in the app settings.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-86_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-87_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="b645ac8b-ec7b-464d-b27e-d0d0bad607cd" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>What is the use of G-sensor?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-89_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-90_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-91_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-ec7b664d-f27e-40d0-bad6-07cd9a1a302c"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">The built-in G-sensor detects impacts or sudden vibrations and automatically locks the current video.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-94_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-95_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="5a92a363-888d-453a-9f4e-dcd1adcd4a7b" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How to choose my memory card?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-97_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-98_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-99_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-888d953a-df4e-4cd1-adcd-4a7b190d7d5f"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> Please use a branded micro SD card, Class 10 / U3, with a capacity of 64GB–256GB, and format it in the GKU GO App before use.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-102_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-103_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="4e1d4567-0554-4da7-8121-535e25593071" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Parking Monitor</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-105_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-106_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-107_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-108_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-109_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="5cb4d90f-c1c0-48ad-b83e-45f9b50b13aa" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How to activate Parking Monitor?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-111_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-112_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-113_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-c4676ab4-e85d-432a-82f8-1402e905515a"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Install the Type-C hardwire kit first, then enable Parking Mode or Parking Collision Detection in the app.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-116_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-117_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="fe31f53b-a489-4f87-b7c9-e48fe5f34252" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How do I know if the dash cam is working properly in Parking Monitor Mode?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-119_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-120_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-121_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-0547cad3-7deb-4ef6-9ded-5308135f3db7"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">When the vehicle is parked, the camera will automatically record and save a locked video if a collision is detected.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-124_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-125_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="0ffd478f-b57b-43bb-bb62-8667e56fe6b6" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>After installing the hardware kit, how many days can parking monitoring work if the car is not started?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-127_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-128_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-129_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-90254588-b664-4e0e-bd66-977e415d0348"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">This depends on the car battery capacity. Parking recording duration can be set to 12h / 24h / 48h / 72h. The hardwire kit will cut power automatically if voltage is too low.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-132_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-133_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="e76a8222-2c4e-4c09-9274-b53872157d9a" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Installation and Usage</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-135_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-136_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-137_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-138_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-139_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="8cd4b654-997e-4c5a-b434-b1273d2b750c" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Can I view the recorded videos on my PC?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-141_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-142_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-143_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-0fa28565-e232-46e2-bb0b-2e397300fcdd"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Yes. Remove the SD card and use a card reader, or play downloaded files using a video player such as VLC.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-146_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-147_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="fabde1d6-0faa-4c0d-b325-622cb03135ca" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Do I need to delete files manually?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-149_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-150_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-151_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-c80921e0-3b17-4a60-b3fd-9c36de259480"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">No. Normal videos are automatically overwritten. Only locked videos require manual deletion.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-154_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-155_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="fea6a996-7945-40e9-a54d-d987c235ba46" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Can I view the video remotely?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-157_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-158_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-159_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-794510e9-654d-4987-8235-ba46b3381dc3"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">No. Remote viewing is not supported. Videos can only be accessed when connected to the dash cam WiFi nearby.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-162_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-163_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="b3381dc3-1d1a-4ce3-b56f-7ba8221f25ec" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Can a power bank be used to power the dash cam?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-165_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-166_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-167_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-1d1aace3-356f-4ba8-a21f-25eca68883f5"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Not recommended. Please use the car charger or hardwire kit to ensure stable power supply.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-170_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-171_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="82a95f85-2406-48cb-b814-22d2aaa447af" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>GPS & Speed</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-173_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-174_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-175_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-176_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-177_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="6ca44908-e89f-4dcf-8d16-087689043e68" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Does dashcam record GPS speed and route?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-179_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-180_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-181_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-b9fe6bbc-df53-4454-902f-6597ce0b13ab"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Yes, when GPS is active it can record speed/location/route for playback.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-184_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-185_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="b2a63202-7150-4711-a3d8-f29f562a03b6" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>GPS isn’t working indoors—why?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-187_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-188_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-189_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-38d54ac1-71b4-4268-ad40-b4025b647687"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">GPS needs an open area to receive satellites. Indoors/garages may block the signal.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-192_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-193_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="b66904c6-5740-4ff2-8622-83856252e02b" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How do I view my driving route (map playback)?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-195_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-196_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-197_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-3fa777be-f0c2-41d4-b6f7-7b3312ad4b30"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Use the app, or use the GKU Player on a computer for GPS track playback.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-200_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-201_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="d7aa6066-f735-4b6b-a42a-b40aced5a9f1" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why don’t I see speed/GPS info on the video?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-203_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-204_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-205_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-f7350b6b-a42a-440a-8ed5-a9f17518cbc5"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Enable Speed Watermark and GPS Coordinates in settings, and give it time to get a GPS lock in an open area.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-208_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-209_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="7518cbc5-95b6-4777-9e70-5b75dbca481d" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 