svg><span>How long is the warranty?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-273_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-274_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-275_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-45c6f446-3aa1-4855-aa93-58d5f04d643a"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">The standard warranty is<strong> 1 year</strong>, and we also provide<strong> lifetime technical support</strong>. If you <strong>register your product</strong>, you can <strong>extend the warranty by 1 additional year</strong> (for a total of<strong> 2 years</strong>).</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-278_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-279_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="b24acbb8-92d9-4ab8-8663-f8138e65a949" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Troubleshooting</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-281_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-282_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-283_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-284_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-285_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="1a6167cb-6a08-4c9a-a7ce-622d59524277" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Time & Recording Issues</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-287_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-288_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-289_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-290_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-291_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="578fe9bd-555a-477d-aeb2-686845b797c9" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The recorded video time does not match the system time. What should I do?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-293_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-294_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-295_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-da43f639-7acf-49d8-a1b3-04d6104582c8"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> Connect the dash cam to the app via WiFi and confirm time sync. Check your phone’s time/time zone. Try a factory reset. If it persists, contact support.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-298_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-299_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="5f41e86a-b92d-4c35-9910-9534b543c876" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Overheating</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-301_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-302_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-303_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-304_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-305_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="05123459-1e7d-4758-b9a9-43c57aa50894" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why does the dash cam get hot during use?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-307_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-308_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-309_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-62403e36-a017-49fb-9857-79ef8324da57"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Mild heat is normal, especially during 4K recording, parking mode, or direct sunlight. The operating range is -4°F to 158°F. If it overheats abnormally, shuts down, or shows a high-temp warning, contact support.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-312_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-313_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="7bd4a0e4-4616-4e11-8931-ad2683f41975" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Power & Recording Problems</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-315_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-316_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-317_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-318_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-319_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="02566c32-ef24-423f-a2f5-008990362c8e" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The dash cam beeps after power-on and does not record.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-321_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-322_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-323_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-9c61eb22-8425-4859-8641-a290162fbd48"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Check the power supply. Test at home using USB-A to USB-C power. Try a different SD card. If it persists, contact support.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-326_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-327_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="ec145aac-45df-4a2d-be9e-b1119f572529" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The dash cam doesn’t record continuously or some videos are missing.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-329_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-330_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-331_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-7c7446fe-1e78-40b5-8cec-de6f25540826"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Ensure stable power. Check both the loop folder and the locked folder. Test at home recording for 1–2 hours with a phone USB charger, then verify in the app. If it persists, contact support.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-334_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-335_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="1d780c5e-1ef2-4d84-8900-1e1f0259f8d2" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>G-Sensor & Voice Alerts</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-337_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-338_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-339_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-340_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-341_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="05f42c6f-a299-4a12-ab8e-9caa75358f66" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why does the dash cam frequently announce “Video Locked”?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-343_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-344_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-345_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-b5b8536c-e1bf-41e2-b57d-c5311f3a1d61"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Connect to WiFi and lower the G-sensor sensitivity if it’s too high. If it persists, contact support and provide the firmware version.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-348_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-349_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="340c6de1-8bc9-4082-8633-e84f396b3747" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Rear Camera Issues</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-351_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-352_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-353_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-354_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-355_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="d95ff0a8-218a-444d-964e-c7e5e5ce5994" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The dash cam can’t detect the rear camera or it doesn’t record.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-357_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-358_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-359_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-e315a316-bedd-4cee-90cb-0fce65392a78"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Reconnect the rear camera firmly before powering on. Unplug power and rear camera, plug the rear camera in first, then power on. Check the rear camera icon in the app. If it persists, contact support.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-362_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-363_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="59a687b0-3af8-4fd0-ba3d-34673ad23046" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Power Issues</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-365_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-366_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-367_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-368_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-369_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="a4ec1b9f-92b8-49f3-9a04-2c4c1695b852" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The dash cam doesn’t turn on.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-371_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-372_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-373_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-d65cd090-52fe-417b-9a27-507dbe8e2308"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Check the power cable and source. Test with a wall charger using USB-A to USB-C. Do not use USB-C to USB-C cable as it may cause compatibility issues. If it still won’t power on, contact support.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-376_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-377_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="a2fa15cf-c0c2-4c8a-9407-5afe05087d6f" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>WiFi Password & Settings</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-379_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-380_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-381_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-382_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-383_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="5595fffd-a43c-4a76-bbd7-54f385769a01" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>What is the default WiFi password?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-385_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-386_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-387_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-892f3b84-3cf2-4e36-b211-d4e8a2d2b563"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">The default password is 12345678</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-390_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-391_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="bb7fe509-a55d-41b1-8d89-4d0a135368d9" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How do I change the WiFi password?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-393_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-394_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-395_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-9ab8d5d7-dfd0-4cfa-9d26-a64da73e7b64"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Reset the dash cam and connect using the default password. In the app go to Camera Settings → WiFi Password. After changing it, forget the old network on your phone and reconnect. Use numbers only.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-398_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-399_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="f4a1e609-54ea-4832-8163-385ace844eb3" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why can’t I reconnect after changing the WiFi password?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-401_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-402_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-403_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-eef5aba6-80db-4646-8105-6c86e549f53c"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Forget the previous dash cam WiFi network in your phone settings and reconnect with the new password. Special characters are not supported.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-406_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-407_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="acea5000-35d6-4b5d-bbd0-c0d4b48e5c73" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Android-Specific</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-409_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-410_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-411_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-412_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-413_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="6ead0c58-a7c8-42e0-a59a-19ee72351a1f" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Android WiFi connection fails or disconnects automatically.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-415_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-416_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-417_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-7f8727e5-cf30-4e31-b81b-b7a211182cef"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">When prompted, select “Stay connected even without internet.” Also disable VPN and nearby car WiFi systems (CarPlay/Android Auto) that may interfere.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-420_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-421_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="1afa3dff-8f3d-4fcd-bf3b-ec463729c168" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Android has no internet after connecting to the dash cam WiFi.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-423_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-424_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-425_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-0c75acb4-d55d-4a42-8556-eee33ee5b6a5"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">This is normal due to Android system behavior. Disconnect from the dash cam WiFi when you need internet. Recording is not affected.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-428_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-429_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="75a0b7ef-dd97-402e-9e4a-ccedc9bbefc2" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> Memory Card (SD Card)</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-431_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-432_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-433_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-434_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-435_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="a08fc44b-cd17-4081-be02-28222095ae57" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> It says “Please format the memory card” / “Card error”. What should I do?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-437_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-438_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-439_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-00bde5e8-67fa-4016-926a-0b6cf8f7aa61"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">  Step-by-step:<br> <br>1) Power on the dash cam and connect your phone to the dash cam WiFi<br><br>2) Open the APP → Settings → Format SD Card<br> <br>3) After formatting, record for 5–10 minutes and check whether new files are created<br> <br>4) If the message returns, remove the card and do a slow format on a computer with a card reader (do not quick format)<br> <br>5) Insert the card back into the dash cam, then format again inside the APP</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-442_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-443_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="e785c9fc-da0b-4db1-a3d3-486fd701e9c3" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> The dash cam beeps after power-on and doesn’t record.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-445_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-446_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-447_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-528c7f3f-293c-4134-a528-a94c7c659818"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br> <br>1) Confirm stable power supply (use the original car charger)<br><br>2) Test the camera at home with a wall charger using USB-A to USB-C<br> <br>3) Replace the memory card and test again<br> <br>4) If it still doesn’t record, format the card in the APP once more</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-450_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-451_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="15230d0a-84f6-4f73-92c1-35d1974f4462" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Some videos are missing / it’s not recording in a loop.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-453_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-454_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-455_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-932f0e43-8fe7-4461-b544-8a46202d5c7b"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br><br>1) Confirm Loop Recording is enabled in settings<br><br>2) Check both folders: - Loop/Normal folder (regular recording) - Locked/Emergency folder (protected clips)<br><br>3) Test recording at home for 1–2 hours with a stable wall charger<br> <br>4) If the locked folder is full (G-sensor too sensitive), lower the G-sensor sensitivity<br> <br>5) If the SD card is near full and loop doesn’t work, back up files and format the card</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-458_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-459_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="2afc6d43-69db-43ca-9e45-238310b77d34" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Video playback fails on PC or shows “playback error”.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-461_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-462_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-463_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-a1c46b62-de3b-4e88-b80b-6f1ab8a2dc92"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br><br>1) Remove the SD card and use a card reader to play the files on a computer <br><br>2) If the files are in TS format, use PotPlayer (or GKU Player) to open them<br> <br>3) If videos play fine on PC, the camera is recording normally and the issue is likely the APP/WiFi connection <br><br>4) If videos also fail on PC, the files may be corrupted — format the card and test again</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-466_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-467_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="3b2d5fc7-e64f-487a-855c-b2a227ed7cdb" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> I use 256GB/512GB and it freezes or becomes unstable.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-469_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-470_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-471_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-f7ba915d-737f-484b-9e12-fcd165669449"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br><br>1) Do a slow format on PC (not quick format)<br> <br>2) Insert into the dash cam and format again in the APP <br><br>3) Use a high-quality card (example: SanDisk Extreme microSD)<br><br>4) If the issue continues, switch to 128GB for best stability</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-474_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-475_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="f443a9d4-46bf-477a-a137-bb31ee481091" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>APP & WiFi</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-477_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-478_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-479_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-480_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-481_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="bb0e5cbd-0cd6-4bef-8d2f-cf7961c165db" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>I connected to WiFi, but it says “No Internet” / “WiFi has no internet access”.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-483_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-484_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-485_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-e2574fc4-2653-4954-8867-5e2a6cc9ae02"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br><br>1) This is normal: dash cam WiFi is a hub-type WiFi for data transfer only<br> <br>2) Keep your phone within 3–5 meters<br> <br>3) Open the APP and add/connect the camera normally</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-488_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-489_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="e7a4c441-538f-419a-894f-2d22406f84a4" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>I can’t connect to the dash cam WiFi.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-491_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-492_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-493_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-438f1d11-e007-4a8d-952e-5be666cc11f9"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br> <br>1) Confirm the dash cam is powered on and recording (indicator light blinking)<br> <br>2) Stand within 3–5 meters<br> <br>3) Turn off: VPN, Bluetooth, mobile data, security/antivirus apps<br> <br>4) On your phone WiFi list, tap the device WiFi and select Forget This Network<br> <br>5) Factory reset the camera (press/hold the function button for &gt;5 seconds)<br> <br>6) Reconnect to device WiFi and enter the default password 12345678 <br><br>7) Open the APP and add the camera</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-496_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-497_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="89320dcb-1ff5-418e-88ac-04fa3cebeff6" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The dash cam WiFi name doesn’t show up (can’t find WiFi).</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-499_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-500_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-501_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-fd50f9da-09dd-40b2-bd43-798700f71548"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br><br>1) Use the original car charger and start the engine to ensure full power<br><br>2) If still not found, do a factory reset (hold the function button &gt;5 seconds)<br> <br>3) Test at home with a wall charger and USB-A to USB-C cable (stable power)<br> <br>4) If it works at home, the vehicle power supply may be unstable</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-504_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-505_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="e856a68e-d4ea-484c-89c6-a4762564a91f" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The APP can’t preview / buffering is slow / can’t download videos.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-507_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-508_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-509_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-e986d377-dd76-4335-9fea-bb9d5c675fe7"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br><br>1) Keep the phone close (within 3–5m) and ensure WiFi is stable<br><br>2) Turn off mobile data while connected to the dash cam WiFi<br> <br>3) For 4K files, download first, then play from your phone gallery to avoid buffering<br> <br>4) If preview/download still fails: - Delete the APP and reinstall the latest version - Test the SD card on a PC via card reader to confirm the files are OK</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-512_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-513_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="f312a0b4-cd6d-40ab-a209-2e558f0a3226" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why can’t I see videos in the APP “Album”?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-515_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-516_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-517_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-ba030dba-63ed-4329-9f6e-dff97bfb10a0"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br> <br>1) The “Album” shows only the files you downloaded to the phone<br><br>2) Connect to dash cam WiFi → open playback → select videos → download<br> <br>3) After download, they will appear in the APP Album / phone gallery</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-520_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-521_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="a5af7a76-ea7a-4f64-88b3-fcd9590da40d" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Parking Monitor</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-523_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-524_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-525_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-526_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-527_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="a30f8f3d-cc3f-497a-919b-034bcc7cc090" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> How do I install the hardwire kit (step-down voltage kit)?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-529_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-530_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-531_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-00370750-0c0b-4755-8933-2df5827b70c6"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "><strong>Step 1: Locate your vehicle’s fuse box</strong><br>Please find your fuse box using your vehicle’s Fuse Box Diagram (owner’s manual or fuse box cover diagram). Please open the fuse box cover. Some covers lift by a small tab; others may require gently prying a panel—please use the included trim tool if needed.<br><br>If you have trouble locating the fuse box, please let us know and we’ll help.<br><br><strong>Step 2: Identify the correct fuse slots (ACC + Constant Power)</strong><br>You will need two fuse slots:<br><br>Constant Power fuse (Yellow wire): provides power all the time, even when the engine is off. (Required for parking mode.)<br><br>ACC fuse (Red wire): provides power only when the key is in ACC/ON. (Used for normal driving recording.)<br><br><strong>Step 3: Connect the Red &amp; Yellow fuse taps (Add-A-Fuse) and verify with a voltmeter</strong><br>Please use a voltmeter to confirm you picked the correct fuse slots:<br><br>Red Wire (ACC): Please turn the car key to the ACC position.Please test the aluminum end of the RED Add-A-Fuse with a voltmeter.If you see voltage, it confirms this slot is powered in ACC.<br><br>Yellow Wire (Constant/B+): Please turn the car off. Please test the aluminum end of the YELLOW Add-A-Fuse with a voltmeter. If you still see voltage, it confirms this slot is constant (always-on) power.<br><br><strong>Step 4: Locate a good ground point (Black wire)<br></strong>Please connect the Black wire (Ground) to a solid metal screw/bolt on the vehicle chassis. We strongly recommend using a proper ground point for stable power.<br><br>Please note: an improper ground connection may cause the dash cam to malfunction or restart intermittently.<br><br>After wiring, please power on the dash cam and confirm it records normally.Please check that Parking Mode appears in the app/settings after a correct hardwire installation. If your fuse type doesn’t match the fuse taps you have, please contact us</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-534_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-535_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="87a95bda-c70e-48da-b865-d53afea7e2d1" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Parking Monitoring option doesn’t appear in the APP.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-537_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-538_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-539_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-1b39e39b-d638-4aec-be10-3b45cfaaa6d5"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step (<strong>wiring verification</strong>):<br> <br>1) Use a multimeter to find the correct fuses: - ACC fuse (for RED wire): - Engine ON: has power - Engine OFF: 0V - BATT/Constant fuse (for YELLOW wire): - Engine ON: has power - Engine OFF: 12V+ <br><br>2) Connect BLACK wire to a metal ground point <br><br>3) Restart the car, power on the dash cam, connect WiFi, and check the APP again <br><br>4) If Parking Monitoring still doesn’t show, re-check fuse selection and wiring</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-542_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-543_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="a523bb66-49ab-41fb-8c11-f5d476659e89" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>After the car is off, I can’t connect to the dash cam WiFi / the camera looks “offline”.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-545_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-546_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-547_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-bc6d49dd-45c1-48e0-8783-b22fdcc5434e"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step: <br><br>1) This can be normal in parking mode: WiFi may be disabled to reduce power and prevent tampering<br><br> 2) To check parking recordings: - Start the car → connect WiFi → open playback - Look for time-lapse files in the loop folder (often with “tlp” in the filename) - Look for collision-triggered files in the locked folder</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-550_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-551_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="78d0a0d7-4ae5-44e1-abe4-81679e9ab9ff" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Time-lapse parking videos play very fast. Is that normal?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-553_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-554_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-555_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-c6ef92ca-5dcb-42d8-af08-8fbf83aee3d8"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step: <br><br>1) Yes. Time-lapse records at a very low frame rate (e.g., 1 frame per second) <br><br>2) That means a short clip may contain a long parking period, so playback looks fast <br><br>3) For better viewing, download the file and play on a PC with PotPlayer</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-558_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-559_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="20c21c1f-9298-481e-8a8e-db31d57570ce" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Will parking mode drain my car battery?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-561_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-562_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-563_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-063e4f78-abe6-44b3-80e2-84835aa8b6f7"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> Step-by-step:<br><br>1) The hardwire kit has low-voltage protection and will cut off power when voltage drops below about 11.8V <br><br>2) Battery drain risk depends on your battery health and how long the car is parked <br><br>3) To reduce risk: - Use Collision Detection mode for long parking - Or set a limited time-lapse duration (e.g., 12h/24h) instead of always-on</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-566_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-567_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="b4eb0cee-9446-44d8-8bf4-c0c2aeb5a6e0" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>After installing the fuse tap, my car’s original function stopped working.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-569_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-570_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-571_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-112beab0-ed49-458c-aeb9-0e0d07ce7be8"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> Step-by-step: <br><br>1) Make sure you inserted the original vehicle fuse back into the fuse tap<br><br>2) The fuse tap has two slots: one for the original circuit fuse, one for the dash cam <br><br>3) After installation, test both the vehicle function and dash cam power</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-574_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-575_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="96377a16-501b-4274-9b1d-7975b7f95061" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>What fuse rating can the hardwire kit use? Can it go into a 15A or higher slot?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-577_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-578_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-579_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-814f9be1-9297-4ca3-8195-a5a5102f7496"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step: <br><br>1) The hardwire kit supports up to 15A <br><br>2) In parking mode, the dash cam current is typically under 700mA <br><br>3) You can use a 15A-or-higher fuse slot as long as that circuit is not shared with other high-load devices</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details></div></div></section></div></div></div><script>
